pth_poll_ev: a negative descriptor is ignored, its revents 0, as POSIX
has poll(); Pth did FD_SET(-1) on its invalid-descriptor set, a write before
the set (libupnp polls -1 for the socket it does not use and crashed).

--- a/pth_high.c
+++ b/pth_high.c
@@ -511,6 +511,8 @@
            data received on a socket", hence we push POLLWRBAND events
            onto wfds instead of efds. Additionally, remember invalid
            filedescriptors in an extra fd_set xfds. */
+        if (pfd[i].fd < 0)
+            continue;   /* POSIX: ignored; FD_SET(-1) would write before the set */
         if (!pth_util_fd_valid(pfd[i].fd)) {
             FD_SET(pfd[i].fd, &xfds);
             continue;
@@ -542,6 +544,8 @@
     n = 0;
     for (i = 0; i < nfd; i++) {
         pfd[i].revents = 0;
+        if (pfd[i].fd < 0)
+            continue;   /* ignored, revents 0 */
         if (FD_ISSET(pfd[i].fd, &xfds)) {
             if (pfd[i].fd >= 0) {
                 pfd[i].revents |= POLLNVAL;
